@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] public-host-starts-before-legacy-authority
The executable public mode MUST be opt-in and return before legacy checkout/state,
account seeding, GitHub CLI/environment credential lookup, agent work, warming and
private HTTP/RPC initialization. Missing personal configuration MUST expose truthful
disabled GitHub discovery without opening personal storage. Configured startup MUST
use only explicit isolated paths, Pully OAuth configuration and private vault-key
files; partial/invalid configuration MUST fail safely, never select legacy authority.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 public/personal isolation plan and 22 Oct executable-listener
completion instruction.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-public-read-is-a-typed-capability
The typed personal GitHub read surface MUST expose only the fixed GET repositories, selected
repository pulls and own-pulls routes under api/personal/v1/github, its separate
account family and typed account capabilities, plus its fixed Account-only review
opening, overview, diff, file-pair and review-data GET routes. A handler
MUST resolve the actual current personal bearer through the canonical auth vault;
caller account/email, cookies, Access credentials and broader inherited OAuth scopes
MUST NOT select authority. Existing public routes MUST retain publicRead authority
and reject private data. Account routes MUST require the session's explicit
privateRepositories capability obtained through actual GitHub repository consent,
and return its captured account/immutable GitHub identity and repository visibility.
No arbitrary RPC, URL or method MAY be forwarded. This intentionally extends the
21 Oct public-first boundary for Tavi's 22 Oct clarification that a signed-in user
must reach their own accessible private repositories and PRs; it MUST NOT silently
broaden existing public sessions or route semantics. The fixed review read extension
implements Tavi's 22 Oct full personal-account app instruction; it grants no arbitrary
RPC, GitHub writes or AI capability.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-read-sources-and-repositories-stay-current
Every awaited GitHub read and final publication MUST retain the original canonical
session/source. PR inventories MUST recheck authorized access and immutable repository
identity before and after reading titles, including public visibility for publicRead,
name-reuse and in-flight sign-out
races. Search selectors MUST come only from verified identity and typed relation;
search issue IDs MUST be revalidated before publication. Credentials and arbitrary
upstream bodies/errors MUST NOT appear in answers. Reads MUST have finite body,
inventory, request, concurrency and whole-route deadlines. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
cross-user/cache/source isolation requirements and 22 Oct real-loopback proof scope.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-repository-denials-retire-older-readers
A confirmed repository access/visibility denial or immutable-ID replacement MUST
retire older in-flight publications for that captured tenant and read capability.
An older metadata response MUST NOT restore the retired repository generation, and
another tenant MUST NOT share that fence. Bounded repository slots MUST accommodate
a normal twenty-repository inbox page without aliases below capacity. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct source-isolation decision and confirmed 22 Oct full-review finding 1.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] own-pull-relations-use-current-immutable-identity
Own-pull search MUST fetch the authenticated GitHub user, match its immutable numeric
ID to the captured session, and use its current validated login. A changed identity
or login before publication MUST deny that old relation rather than label another
user's search results with the original subject. Email/login matching MUST NOT
replace numeric identity. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct per-user GitHub requirement and
confirmed 22 Oct full-review finding 4 about rename and old-login reassignment.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] own-pull-draft-comes-from-authoritative-state
An optional or stale search draft value MUST NOT overwrite fresh issue/PR state.
When the fresh issue omits draft, the handler MUST obtain it from that pull's fixed
endpoint and validate its number and immutable base repository before publication.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct actual own-PR inventory requirement and confirmed 22 Oct
full-review finding 2 about indexed draft and optional GitHub search fields.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] public-auth-is-not-global-ai-eligibility
GitHub authentication MUST govern only GitHub/account capabilities, not whether a
person may configure or use AI. A verified non-GitHub AI/local principal or explicitly
labelled service-default allowance MUST remain a separate capability with its own
credential and budget boundaries. Public mode MUST NOT silently adopt private owner
GitHub credentials, CLI homes or a paid provider after a personal failure. The typed-read slice
MUST NOT claim paid AI execution or provider-subscription connectivity. The separate
trusted workspace MAY connect the account's own Claude/Codex subscription as specified
by Tavi25Oct2026, without changing typed-read or guest authority. Source: Tavi's
22 Oct 2026 clarification that AI does not require GitHub and the approved provider
connection plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] workspace-rpc-is-separate-from-typed-personal-reads
The separate /workspace/api/rpc route MUST admit only the fixed native phone methods and
canonical account/provider-login operations, bounded in method, body, concurrency and
request lifetime. It MUST return the existing result/error-string envelope and no-store
responses, and MUST NOT accept arbitrary browser storage, raw prompts, GitHub proxy,
provider URLs, legacy sessions or cookies. Cloudflare Access headers MAY accompany this
route but MUST NOT authenticate an account or become GitHub headers. The older typed
personal/public paths MUST retain their existing authority and header rules. Source:
Tavi25Oct2026, one GitHub login opening the full production native workspace.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] workspace-cached-private-content-rechecks-current-repository
Before publishing cached diffs, full files, saved reviews/tours, list entries or task
results, workspace requests MUST revalidate the selected repository with the captured
personal GitHub credential and immutable repository ID. Denial, name replacement or
captured-session revocation MUST prevent the cached content from reaching the client.
Source: Tavi25Oct2026 own-account workspace and existing source-isolation requirements.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] workspace-task-publication-keeps-complete-provenance
Completed and running task wait/list responses MUST reauthorize every server-selected
context repository against its captured immutable ID, including Inbox tasks without a
diff record and repositories absent from answer citations. Caller hints and answer text
MUST NOT supply that provenance. Missing provenance MUST fail closed. Source: confirmed
ce-code-review finding 4 and Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 assigned fix batch.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] workspace-repository-checks-share-bounded-concurrency
Workspace publication MUST deduplicate case-insensitive repository names within each
validation phase and validate distinct repositories concurrently within the existing
three-request GitHub permit budget. It MUST retain current access, immutable-ID checks
and a final check of every captured repository lease after all awaited validation.
Source: confirmed ce-code-review finding 5 and Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 assigned fix batch.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] workspace-transient-admission-does-not-reject-session
Workspace RPC and event admission MUST reserve 401 for rejected, unconfirmed or
reconnect-required personal sessions, use 403 for insufficient authority, and preserve
temporary provider, vault storage, context and capacity failures as retryable 503 or
429 responses. The native error-string envelope and any known Retry-After MUST remain
intact. Source: confirmed ce-code-review finding 3 and Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 assigned fix batch.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] workspace-events-are-sanitized-and-owned
The fixed POST /workspace/api/events route MUST require the same previously confirmed
canonical privateRepositories personal-vault session and captured source as workspace
RPC. It MUST ingest only through the existing Analytics sanitizer and batch policy,
retain the 2 MiB request bound, and answer 204 on success. Its events MUST live only in
the immutable personal account's durable analytics scope, respecting the existing
opt-out and retention policy; Access-only, missing, revoked, public-only, cookie and
legacy-session authority MUST NOT write events or use the legacy analytics queue.
Source: Tavi25Oct2026 full owned Stats/usage integration refinement.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] workspace-does-not-issue-unusable-agent-keys
Workspace RPC MUST refuse agent-key-create while personal agent-key ingress is absent.
Existing key list/revoke MAY remain for cleanup. ExistingServer key creation and its
/api/v1 behavior MUST remain unchanged. This phone-workspace restoration MUST NOT add
an agent ingress, key-owner locator, new key lifetime or public transport interface.
Source: Tavi25Oct2026 integration decision to keep personal Settings truthful about
unavailable agent submissions after inspecting the existing full Settings workflow.
